<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valletta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valletta is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a>, built on the Sciberras peninsula between two harbours. It was founded in 1566 by Grand Master <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-parisot-de-valette">Jean de Valette</a> after the Ottoman Great Siege, as a fortified city for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a>, and became their capital in 1571. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> churches, palaces and bastions made it a World Heritage Site in 1980.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valletta.jpg" alt="Valletta" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mandyy88 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Sebastian_Curtain_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
